From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kieran Drewett <kieran@drewett.dev>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 03:12:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] meson: expose Wayland support in generated config

The Gnoblin Mutter build sets HAVE_WAYLAND in Meson's configuration, but the
macro is absent from config.h.meson. Without the template entry, Wayland-gated
runtime hooks compile as no-ops even though the compositor is built with
Wayland.

---
 config.h.meson | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/config.h.meson b/config.h.meson
index 5e7e09b10..a9f5b3999 100644
--- a/config.h.meson
+++ b/config.h.meson
@@ -37,6 +37,9 @@
 /* libwacom has get_num_rings() */
 #mesondefine HAVE_LIBWACOM_GET_NUM_RINGS
 
+/* Define if the Wayland compositor is enabled */
+#mesondefine HAVE_WAYLAND
+
 /* Define if you want to enable XWayland support */
 #mesondefine HAVE_XWAYLAND
 
